<title>PERU: Peru's October wheat output falls 32.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's October wheat output falls 32.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's October wheat production fell 32.5 percent to 8,821 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>Output for the first ten months, however, was up to 139,219 tonnes from 120,858 tonnes in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Total 1995 wheat production was 125,048 tonnes.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in October rose 29.1 percent to $29.0 million, compared with the same month last year, while in the first ten months they rose 45.6 percent to $207.3 million, compared with the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
